# Copy to .env for local builds. .env is gitignored — never commit real values.
# The same two variables must also be set in the Vercel project settings, or
# production deploys fall back to the written reviews.
#
# Both are read at BUILD TIME only (src/data/googleReviews.ts). Neither is
# exposed to the browser: they have no PUBLIC_ prefix, so Astro keeps them
# server-side.

# Google Cloud console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials.
# Enable "Places API (New)" on the project, then restrict this key to that one
# API so a leak cannot be spent against Maps, Routes or Geocoding.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# The Place ID for Lisa's Google Business listing. Find it with the Place ID
# Finder: https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/place-id
# Looks like: ChIJN1t_tDeuEmsRUsoyG83frY4
GOOGLE_PLACE_ID=
